{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112103,"nonce":"MVkP4Yny5dx9MMauxgQyrrFmrM0=","title":"4.2 Play-loop skill","message":"Wave 4 — play. Depends: 1.3, 1.4, 2.1, 4.1. Packaging, not invention.\n\n## Goal\nThe play loop as a reusable skill/prompt: how an agent session actually runs\na colony — cadence, checklist discipline, escalation, artifacts.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- DESIGN.md (the loop, four layers); 4.1 (playbook contract);\n  1.4 (transcripts, watch)\n- Workspace skill conventions (how /triage-errors and friends are structured)\n\n## Scope\nA skill (or prompt doc if skills don't fit the runner) encoding:\n- Session start: load playbook INDEX + checklists + landmarks + last digest;\n  `rwa status`; resume or newgame per args.\n- The loop: morning checklist at each in-game day start; act; advance with\n  until-guards (any-letter default, max one in-game day per advance early\n  on); digest+journal read; think; repeat. Long advances announced when\n  watched (`rwa watch` status).\n- Emergency posture: on threat letters — verify SeekAndKill engagement, only\n  then intervene (draft) by exception.\n- Artifacts: run-dir transcript, daily digest snapshots, end-of-session\n  summary + post-mortem when a loss occurred.\n- Escalation to Dorian: colony-ending events, spec gaps, anything requiring\n  installs it must not touch.\n\n## Invariants\nThe skill never bypasses rwa (no direct file pokes); checklist items always\nproduce either \"ok\" or an action — silent skips forbidden.\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nSkill vs prompt-doc packaging; cadence tuning (advance sizes); how much state\npersists between sessions beyond playbook (a COLONY-NOTES.md?).\n\n## Acceptance\nA scripted one-day session on a fixture colony: checklist artifacts produced,\nat least one checklist-driven action taken, transcript complete, summary\nwritten. Reviewed against the skill text for compliance.","files":null}]}